How can you delete the duplicate records?

Table orders has duplicate records based on order_id

1️⃣ Create a clean table (remove duplicates)
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE orders_clean AS
SELECT *
FROM (
    SELECT *,
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY order_id ORDER BY order_date DESC) AS rn
    FROM orders
)
WHERE rn = 1;

2️⃣ Swap tables
ALTER TABLE orders SWAP WITH orders_clean;

👉 What happens: orders now has clean data
*****Note: Old data moves to orders_clean (backup)

3️⃣ Drop backup (optional)
DROP TABLE orders_clean;
✅ Why Use SWAP?
Very fast (metadata operation ⚡)
No downtime
Safe rollback (before dropping backup)
No heavy DELETE operations
